# H2 (run 2 of 3): the AUDITS-OFF HANG SHAPES at eight seats on c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-best-time-gate (the nine levers, the quad blocks, the in-trace sampler hang fix, 262k windows). The shapes:
# concurrent4_steady, concurrent8_steady (the quad blocks' mix), steady_resend (an engine build after many packed rounds), replay_concurrent4 and replay_concurrent8 (a rows=2 sequential replay), and the
# exactness reference concurrent8_code_equal, then the split-block and drain shapes. Each run follows its own all-four reset. READ: three CONSECUTIVE completions (H1 to H3), every user at budget,
# c2_smoke_check clean (two quad markers, a both-quads round, no fallback), no watchdog or replay-deadline exit, the concurrent8_code_equal hashes equal in every run and equal to S0's. No stall watch on
# this profile: a stall waits for the job timeout and records nothing, which is itself the finding. Duration (estimate): 90 min. Stop rule: one stall stops the window.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/262k8 eight-seat 262k development window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/262k8 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a
# registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch by its author.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-262k8-best-1 is what B0 builds from the pushed tp4/262k8 commit; every later job serves that one image. A commit of a
# file the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. The cards are under development: this window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-262k8-best-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-best-time-gate
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,concurrent4_steady,concurrent8_steady,steady_resend,replay_concurrent4,replay_concurrent8,concurrent8_code_equal,concurrent5_split,concurrent8_drain
